# XSH cproj(), cprojf() and cprojl()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only what the page makes exact is tested: values returned unchanged or with
# a stated sign change, including signed zeros, infinities and NaN parts.
# Arguments are built with CMPLX() and pass through volatile objects, and the
# three types (name, name with f, name with l) are each tested. Infinite and
# NaN cases are skipped where the type has none.

assertion  XSH.cproj.001
anchor     functions/cproj.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cproj.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cproj of a value with no infinite part is that value: finite
           values, zeros with their signs (for a type with negative zero), and
           values with a NaN part, parts unchanged.
test       t/001-non-infinite.c

assertion  XSH.cproj.002
anchor     functions/cproj.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cproj.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cproj of a value whose real part is +Inf or -Inf, with any
           imaginary part (finite, zero, infinite or NaN), is +Inf with an
           imaginary part that is a zero carrying the sign of the imaginary
           part (either sign for a NaN).
test       t/002-infinite-real.c

assertion  XSH.cproj.003
anchor     functions/cproj.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cproj.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cproj of a value whose imaginary part is +Inf or -Inf, with any
           real part (finite, zero or NaN), is +Inf with an imaginary part
           that is +0 or -0 following the sign of the infinite part.
test       t/003-infinite-imag.c
